  "id": "Compound::DB00544 - Disease::DOID:4159",
  "verbalization": "Fluorouracil is implicated in the development of Skin Cancer through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Fluorouracil causes Ichthyosis or Ichthyosis Acquired, which in turn is associated with Bleomycin, a chemotherapeutic agent that treats Skin Cancer. This indicates a potential causal link between Fluorouracil and Skin Cancer via the intermediate step of Bleomycin. The shared lowest common ancestor of Fluorouracil and Bleomycin as a Cytotoxic Chemotherapeutic Agent and Heteroorganic Entity suggests a broader biological context where these agents may interact in a manner that influences cancer development. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Fluorouracil in initiating a cascade that ultimately leads to Skin Cancer, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
